<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · China, Tibet and Mongolia</p><h1 class="st-title">Kingdom of Hengshan</h1><p class="st-meta">206 BCE – 202 BCE · capital Zhu</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Wu Rui's kingdom in the middle Yangtze, created by Xiang Yu in 206 BCE, whose ruler switched to Liu Bang and became the first King of Changsha.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wu-rui">Wu Rui</a>, a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/qin-dynasty">Qin</a> magistrate of Po county who was popular with the Yue peoples, joined the rebellion against the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/qin-dynasty">Qin dynasty</a> and sent troops with his son-in-law <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ying-bu">Ying Bu</a>. In 206 BCE <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/xiang-yu">Xiang Yu</a> made him King of Hengshan, with his capital at Zhu near modern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/huanggang">Huanggang</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hubei">Hubei</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Hengshan straddled the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yangtze-river">Yangtze</a> east of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-linjiang">Kingdom of Linjiang</a>, controlling <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rice">rice</a> lands and river trade. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wu-rui">Wu Rui's</a> support among the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/baiyue">Baiyue</a> peoples of the south gave him a following beyond the Chinese population.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wu-rui">Wu Rui</a> supported <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/liu-bang">Liu Bang</a> against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/xiang-yu">Xiang Yu</a>, and after the Han victory in 202 BCE he was moved to become King of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/changsha">Changsha</a>. His family held Changsha until 157 BCE, one of the few non-Liu kingdoms to survive under the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/han-dynasty">Han Dynasty</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="kingdom, 206 BCE – 202 BCE"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M22 72 V40 L36 54 L50 28 L64 54 L78 40 V72 Z"/><path d="M22 80 H78"/><circle cx="50" cy="24" r="3"/><circle cx="22" cy="36" r="2.5"/><circle cx="78" cy="36" r="2.5"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">kingdom</p><p class="st-emblem-region">China, Tibet and Mongolia</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:55.60%;width:1.20%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>206 BCE – 202 BCE</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/3rd-century-bce">3rd century BCE</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>kingdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Zhu</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Wu Rui</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Chinese ancestral religion</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Old Chinese</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/china">China</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Hengshan (Wu Rui)</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=-204&amp;focus=kingdom-of-hengshan" aria-label="Kingdom of Hengshan on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="7398 1013 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Kingdom of Hengshan lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M7909 1324h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M7718 1269h0"/><path class="map-dot-ap" d="M7718 1269h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>Location approximate: shown in present-day China. <a href="/atlas?year=-204&amp;focus=kingdom-of-hengshan">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>

